Pass a regex to replace, optionally with the g flag for all occurrences, and reference capture groups with $1 and friends.

code:
console.log('2026-01-05'.replace(/(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})/, '$3/$2/$1'));
// 05/01/2026

real example:
Normalizing date formats scraped from varying locales before comparison is done with a regex replace.

Playwright matchers accept regex where strings are expected, so text, attribute, and URL checks support patterns.

code:
await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\/checkout\?step=\d+/);
await expect(page.getByText(/order confirmed/i)).toBeVisible();

real example:
Asserting a redirect URL pattern instead of an exact URL keeps assertions stable across query param order.
